How do I configure memory limits, worker threads, and spill-to-disk directory for out-of-core queries on `ride_trips` in DuckDB (variant 1)?

### Answer:
```sql
SET memory_limit = '12GB';
SET threads = 8;
SET max_temp_directory_size = '100GB';
SET temp_directory = '/mnt/nvme/duckdb_temp';
SET preserve_insertion_order = false;

EXPLAIN ANALYZE
SELECT pickup_loc, SUM(dropoff_loc)
FROM ride_trips
GROUP BY ALL;
```

### Explanation:
DuckDB handles workloads exceeding RAM by streaming partitions to the designated `temp_directory`.

